g placed other participants between them, then at least one adjacent pair in that chain must also have reversed. The smallest budget over adjacent pairs therefore lower-bounds the budget of any non-adjacent reversal, and adjacent pairs are the cheapest rank events. \\emph{Top and mid:} the top pair is the position that leaderboards publicise, and the mid pair probes a typical interior position. \\emph{A 2\\% cap:} it fixes a common tolerance for how much of a table noise or an actor could plausibly alter and makes scores comparable across tables of different size. It is a convention of the evaluator, not an estimate of any real process, and we did not vary it; all held-out budgets sit well below it except the sports top pair, which uses 24\\% of its allowance. % @evidence[[derived/final_stats.json#cases.F3.k_over_cap]]\n245:\\paragraph{What it does not support.} (i) \\emph{No causal claim about evaluation design.} Crowd votes and sports are confounded with table size, participants, era, outcome granularity and tie structure; one table per design means the contrast cannot be separated from table identity. (ii) \\emph{No claim about expert or model-judge designs on held-out data.} The only expert-design evidence is a six-model development table with no flip within the cap and an unknown cause; no model-judge data were evaluated. (iii) \\emph{No superiority claim.} The studied configuration equals influence-only removal in every case, and the starting baseline was not run on held-out tables. The qualified outcome of the held-out evaluation certifies that the evaluation completed with its controls passing; it neither establishes that the configuration is better nor extends findings beyond four cases. (iv) \\emph{No rank-uncertainty or manipulation claim.} A flip here is a reversal of a point-estimate order for one adjacent pair. We examine neither confidence-interval-based rank sets, nor insertion, label flipping or rigging by an adversary, nor other rating models; an adversary can usually do more than delete rows, and a platform's published rank may rest on other statistics. (v) \\emph{Limited uncertainty.} Two identical episodes, 20 random draws, and four cases do not support significance statements, and we compute no intervals over data sets.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
